One of the more important things to remember is bear markets don't just start and pull everything lower.

@sonusvarghese looked at the tech bust and found the S&P 500 fell 11% from April to December 2000, yet low volatility stocks soared 32%.

For more than two years now we've had exposure to both low vol and momentum names in the models we run.

